{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43788526",
      "title": "Listening to Events with Event Binding",
      "lectureOrder": 26,
      "videoOrder": 22,
      "sourceHash": "22866b5b1d20967fa4c4efb07486e64e8e5d51f13372640d22f74573532e92a0",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.48,
          "end": 3.12,
          "en": "Now when building web applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.12,
          "end": 5.94,
          "en": "and their user interfaces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.94,
          "end": 9.18,
          "en": "outputting dynamic data is just one thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.18,
          "end": 11.07,
          "en": "you often need to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.07,
          "end": 15.18,
          "en": "You also often need to listen to user input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.18,
          "end": 17.43,
          "en": "so that you can then, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.43,
          "end": 21.363,
          "en": "also update the UI upon certain kinds of input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.29,
          "end": 24.84,
          "en": "And that's, therefore, what we'll do next,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.84,
          "end": 28.05,
          "en": "listen to user input and then in a second step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.05,
          "end": 32.49,
          "en": "also change the UI after some user input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.49,
          "end": 34.86,
          "en": "And conveniently, we have this button here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.86,
          "end": 39.51,
          "en": "So let's say for a start, we'd like to add an event listener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.51,
          "end": 42.72,
          "en": "to that button to listen for click events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.72,
          "end": 44.52,
          "en": "so that we then, for the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.52,
          "end": 47.43,
          "en": "simply output something in the console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.43,
          "end": 51.33,
          "en": "And in Angular where you write declarative code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.33,
          "end": 53.91,
          "en": "you add event listeners to elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.91,
          "end": 57.42,
          "en": "by going to those elements in your templates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.42,
          "end": 59.94,
          "en": "So by going to this button, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.94,
          "end": 62.67,
          "en": "and by then specifying the name of the event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.67,
          "end": 63.72,
          "en": "you wanna listen to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.72,
          "end": 65.91,
          "en": "So for example, click.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.91,
          "end": 70.14,
          "en": "You then wrap this event name with parentheses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.14,
          "end": 73.89,
          "en": "regular parentheses, opening and closing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.89,
          "end": 76.14,
          "en": "So event name between parentheses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.14,
          "end": 78.3,
          "en": "That's Angular's syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.3,
          "end": 80.94,
          "en": "for adding an event listener to an element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.94,
          "end": 83.313,
          "en": "to this button here, in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.33,
          "end": 86.7,
          "en": "Now as mentioned, you could add a broad variety",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.7,
          "end": 87.81,
          "en": "of event listeners,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.81,
          "end": 91.08,
          "en": "and if you add an empty pair of parentheses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.08,
          "end": 93.47999999999999,
          "en": "and you place your cursor between them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.47999999999999,
          "end": 95.94,
          "en": "and you press Control + Space,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 95.94,
          "end": 98.64,
          "en": "most IDEs should give you a list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 98.64,
          "end": 100.743,
          "en": "of event listeners you could add.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102,
          "end": 103.68,
          "en": "So here you see the click event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 103.68,
          "end": 105.39,
          "en": "but also a bunch of other events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 105.39,
          "end": 108.06,
          "en": "you could possibly also wanna listen to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 108.06,
          "end": 110.31,
          "en": "In my case here, it's the click event though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 111.36,
          "end": 113.37,
          "en": "Well, and then you should add an equal sign.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 113.37,
          "end": 116.72999999999999,
          "en": "And then between those quotes, you add the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 116.72999999999999,
          "end": 120.24,
          "en": "that should be executed when that event occurs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 120.24,
          "end": 123.6,
          "en": "Though typically, you don't add it here in the template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 123.6,
          "end": 126.24,
          "en": "but instead inside of some method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 126.24,
          "end": 130.05,
          "en": "that you define on your component class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 130.05,
          "end": 131.67,
          "en": "And that's what I'll do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 131.67,
          "end": 134.94,
          "en": "In that user component class, I'll add a new method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 134.94,
          "end": 139.2,
          "en": "and I'll name it onSelectUser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 139.2,
          "end": 141.15,
          "en": "though the name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 141.15,
          "end": 144.69,
          "en": "It's just one common pattern that you'll see quite a bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 144.69,
          "end": 148.41,
          "en": "that those functions, those methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 148.41,
          "end": 151.11,
          "en": "that are meant to be executed upon some event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 151.11,
          "end": 154.5,
          "en": "start with on as a prefix to make it clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 154.5,
          "end": 157.68,
          "en": "that they're meant to be executed upon some event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 157.68,
          "end": 160.82999999999998,
          "en": "But it's not a hard rule you have to follow,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 160.82999999999998,
          "end": 162.78,
          "en": "and you'll see different conventions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 162.78,
          "end": 165.63,
          "en": "in different Angular projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 165.63,
          "end": 168.57,
          "en": "Then you add parentheses and curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 168.57,
          "end": 171.93,
          "en": "And with that, you got a regular method as you could add it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 171.93,
          "end": 176.01,
          "en": "to any class when using TypeScript or JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 176.01,
          "end": 177.69,
          "en": "And here for the moment, I'll then simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 177.69,
          "end": 179.037,
          "en": "console.log('Clicked'),",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 180.12,
          "end": 182.523,
          "en": "just so that we can see that it worked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 183.72,
          "end": 186.03,
          "en": "Now to connect this to the click event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 186.03,
          "end": 189.09,
          "en": "you should use that name of that method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 189.09,
          "end": 193.68,
          "en": "and then use that as a value for this click event listener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 193.68,
          "end": 197.553,
          "en": "and add parentheses after it as if you would be calling it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 198.75,
          "end": 202.2,
          "en": "It will, however, be called for you when that click occurs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 202.2,
          "end": 204.66,
          "en": "not when this line of code is parsed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 204.66,
          "end": 207.12,
          "en": "but instead, only once I click",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 207.12,
          "end": 208.953,
          "en": "on that button element occurred.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 210.42000000000002,
          "end": 214.86,
          "en": "Well, and with that, if you now save that and you go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 214.86,
          "end": 217.29,
          "en": "and you open your developer tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 217.29,
          "end": 219.66,
          "en": "and there your JavaScript Console",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 219.66,
          "end": 222.15,
          "en": "so that you can see log messages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 222.15,
          "end": 226.263,
          "en": "If you click that element, you should see clicked here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 227.16,
          "end": 229.68,
          "en": "And you will see a new output,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 229.68,
          "end": 232.59,
          "en": "as you can tell by this number here, which is changing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 232.59,
          "end": 234.78300000000002,
          "en": "every time I'm clicking this button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 235.65,
          "end": 238.98,
          "en": "And that's how you can listen to events in Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 238.98,
          "end": 242.01,
          "en": "and how you can define which code should execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 242.01,
          "end": 243.033,
          "en": "when they occur.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
